Array : 
--------
1. Array is a collection of homogenous(same type) and heterogenous(different types) data elements
2. Array is a non primitive datatype 
3. Array works on the concept of indexing 
4. Array indexing always starts from zero because it follows number system
5. Array elements shares same name but differentiable by there indexing.
6. Prerequisite for array allocation is base address 
7. Array works on continous memory allocation
8. Types of array : 
    a. One dimensional array
    b. Two dimensional array 
        |-- It have a special type of 2d array which is considered as jazzed array 
        |-- Here in case of jazzed array, we have possibility of different columns with respect to each row
    c. Multi dimensional array